{
  "version": 1,
  "claim": "A fixed-pose compliance probe (sensor force stepped to 2x/3x at the last pose of each sweep direction, other lines held) estimates the true/configured stiffness ratio k on HP3 within about ±4%; feeding probe k into a home-stretch term removes the stiffness/home-reference D.z and low-z error (D.z gap to true-stiffness fit ≤0.041 mm; worst-coordinate error 1.07→0.44 mm on average), at ~3% time cost. A wrong stiffness moves D.z strongly only on HP5 pulley-reduced sweeps and in the ellipsoid shape.",
  "scope": "Simulation only. HP3 live runs (9, true stiffness x0.8-1.2, some with random geometry) refitted offline; slope scans on existing nominal datasets for HP3/HP4/HP5/HP5r. No hardware.",
  "limitations": [
    "Fit change only tested as offline refit; live sweep selection/stopping used today's fit",
    "Only HP3 live",
    "Motor cogging ±0.36 N leaves -0.35..+0.65 mm D.z",
    "Frame convention: origin below D, Dx=Dy=0"
  ],
